# The wave crosses unknown cells as cheaply as walked ones, so a smelled source behind unexplored ground draws the agent straight across terrain that is often wall, and it wastes ticks bumping and re-routing. Here the wave pays an extra toll to cross cells that are neither known free nor known solid (distrust of the unseen), so routes run through known-free ground and the agent reaches food on paths that exist, while the frontier itself (a source on the unknown edge) still pulls through the void weighting of the best law.

channel source
channel solid
channel free
channel thing
channel value
channel void: init 0
channel confinement
channel injection
channel toll

# How much undiscovered country surrounds a cell, diffused and remembered.
rule unknown_mass:
  when 1
  set void = clamp(0.7 * avg8(void) + 0.3 * (1 - free) * (1 - solid), 0, 1)

# Local confinement, as in the best law.
rule calc_conf:
  when 1
  set confinement = sum8(solid)

# The fraction of the wave a cell passes on: an unknown cell is distrusted.
rule distrust:
  when 1
  set toll = 1 - 0.08 * (1 - free) * (1 - solid)

# A source is worth more where a lot of unknown lies behind it; nooks count less.
rule inject:
  when 1
  set injection = max(thing, source * (0.5 + 1.5 * void)) / (1.3 + 0.5 * confinement)

# The Bellman wave, slower through the unknown.
rule wave:
  when 1
  set value = max(injection, toll * max(0.94 * max4(value), 0.916214 * max8(value))) * (1 - solid * (1 - leak))
